        "original_id": "e563c8be-a0a3-5fa3-bdbe-8daba449e7e9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Downton, Herefordshire, Downton-on-the-Rock, England, Wales\n- Concepts: civil parishes, Domesday Book, place names\n\nFacts:\n- In 1086, the Domesday Book, the \"Great Survey\" of much of England and parts of Wales, referred to Downton as \"Duntune.\"\n- The name \"Duntune\" meant \"hill settlement.\"\n- Downton is a civil parish in northern Herefordshire.\n- Downton contains the village of Downton-on-the-Rock.",
