        "original_id": "d13737a4-2a9c-5101-9ad4-90edefbe65aa",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Downton, Herefordshire\n- Works: Domesday Book\n- People: King William the Conqueror\n- Concepts: Place names, Great Survey\n\nFacts:\n- In 1086, the Domesday Book was completed as a manuscript record of the Great Survey of much of England and parts of Wales by order of King William the Conqueror.\n- The Domesday Book is also known in Latin as \"Liber de Wintonia,\" meaning \"Book of Winchester.\"\n- In the Domesday Book, Downton in Herefordshire is recorded as \"Duntune.\"\n- The name \"Duntune\" means \"hill settlement.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
